meta {
  name: Beta Signup
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{protocol}}://{{baseUrl}}/profile/beta-signup
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Origin: http://localhost:3000
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "ios": true,
    "android": false
  }
}

docs {
  Opts the currently authenticated user into the internal mobile test track
  (iOS and/or Android), writing directly to their Auth0 user_metadata.

  Idempotent per platform — resubmitting a platform that's already opted in
  is a no-op (no Auth0 write, no GitHub notification). Notifies via a GitHub
  issue (label `mobile-test-user-opt-in`) that includes the user's display
  name and Auth0 user ID only — never their email.

  ## Authentication
  Requires a valid Bearer token (inherited from collection).

  ## Prerequisites
  The server must be configured with Auth0 M2M credentials:
  - `AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_ID`
  - `AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_SECRET`

  GitHub notification is best-effort — the endpoint still works without
  GitHub credentials configured, it just skips the notification.

  ## Request Body
  - `ios` (boolean, optional, default false): Opt into the iOS test track
  - `android` (boolean, optional, default false): Opt into the Android test track
  - At least one of `ios`/`android` must be true

  ## Responses
  - `200`: Opt-in state reflects the user's current overall opt-in status
    ```json
    {
      "optInTestTrackIos": true,
      "optInTestTrackAndroid": false
    }
    ```
  - `400`: Neither `ios` nor `android` was true
  - `401`: Authentication required or invalid token
}
